            <ArticleTitle>Botulinum toxin for meralgia paresthetica in type 2 diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.dsx.2013.02.028</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1871-4021(13)00029-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Botulinum toxin has been used for a variety of neuropathic conditions in diabetes mellitus. Meralgia paresthetica is a mononeuropathy of femoral nerve seen in diabetes and obesity with an unclear etiopathogenesis. We studied the role of botulinum toxin in resistant cases of meralgia paresthetica in type 2 diabetes.</AbstractText>
